    dcterms:abstract "Social network analysis (SNA) is not a formal theory in sociology but rather strategy for investigating social structures. As it an idea that can be applied many fields, we study, particular, its influence the information sciences. Information scientists study publication, citation and co-citation networks, collaboration structures other forms of interaction networks. Moreover, Internet represents unprecedented scale. In all these studies successfully applied. SNA further related to recent theories concerning free market economy, geography transport The growth documented co-author drawn. Centrality measures are calculated."@pt ;
