<https://doi.org/10.2753/mis0742-1222240302> a bibo:Document ;
    dcterms:abstract "The paper motivates, presents, demonstrates in use, and evaluates a methodology for conducting design science (DS) research information systems (IS). DS is of importance discipline oriented to the creation successful artifacts. Several researchers have pioneered IS, yet over past 15 years, little has been done within discipline. lack serve as commonly accepted framework template its presentation may contributed slow adoption. (DSRM) presented here incorporates principles, practices, procedures required carry out such meets three objectives: it consistent with prior literature, provides nominal process model doing research, mental presenting evaluating IS. includes six steps: problem identification motivation, definition objectives solution, development, demonstration, evaluation, communication. We demonstrate evaluate by four case studies terms DSRM, including cases that present database support health assessment methods, software reuse measure, an Internet video telephony application, IS planning method. designed effectively satisfies potential help aid acceptance"@pt ;
